:: S: Reading (Activity) [storylet]
{=

(storylet: when
(passage:)'s name is $place's stay
)
(metadata:
"title", "Read Something",
"cardDesc", "A scholar always has with them textbooks to study, letters to open, or documents with fine prints to inspect, but rarer is the time to do all of that. Perhaps now is one such times.",
"img", "https://images.fallenlondon.com/icons/book.png",
)
(urgency: -1)


$cssColumnParent[

$cssColumnChild[

    (css: "font-size: 70%")[
        $cssColumnChild[(link: "⇦ Never mind.")[(goto: $place's sublocation)]]
    ]

	$cssBox[
    	($funcImage: (passage:)'s img)
         $cssBoxItem[''(print: (passage:)'s title )''<br>(print: (passage:)'s cardDesc)]
    ]
]

$cssColumnChild[

It is said that writing is one of the earliest forms of magic, wherein a human's cognition is made into matter. This is, of course, hyperbole - yet another form of magic, wherein things are enlarged through say-so alone. 
<br>
$cssDesc[Read documents from your inventory to better understand the world, learn magical formulas, or simply to pass the time.]
<br>
---

<!--No need to build a list. Just feed the entire inventory to $funcReadingList, and it will automatically filter out non-documents-->

($funcReadingList: (datanames: $char's player's inv))


<ol>
<br>Actually...
<li>(link: "Never mind.")[(goto: $place's sublocation)]
</ol>

]<!--end child-->
]<!--end parent-->